		<title type="html"><![CDATA[Réponse à&#160;:  Migration Vues Oracle avec jointures externes.]]></title>
		<link rel="alternate" href="http://forums.postgresql.fr/viewtopic.php?pid=1620#p1620"/>
		<content type="html"><![CDATA[<p>Je ne l&#039;ai évidemment pas vérifié ...</p><p>SELECT p_entity.ENTITY_INCDE,ENTITY_DSC,RESULT_INCDE,ENTITY_GO_INCDE,DOC_AUTHOR,RESULT_REAL_DTE,RESULT_TYPE_INCDE,REF_EXCDE <br />&#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160;FROM p_resultat <br />&#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160;JOIN p_entity <br />&#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160;ON (p_entity.entity_incde = p_resultat.result_incde)<br />&#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160;JOIN r_go <br />&#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160;ON (p_entity.entity_go_incde = r_go.go_incde)<br />&#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160;LEFT JOIN r_resultat_type rr <br />&#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160;ON (p_resultat.RESULT_TYPE_INCDE =&#160; rr.REF_INCDE)<br />&#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160;LEFT JOIN&#160; a_entity_document aed <br />&#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160;ON (p_entity.entity_incde =&#160; aed.ENTITY_INCDE)<br />&#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160;LEFT JOIN p_document doc <br />&#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160;ON (aed.DOC_INCDE = doc.DOC_INCDE)<br />WHERE<br />&#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160;p_entity.entity_status_incde = 4 <br />&#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160;AND p_entity.entity_sec_lvl = 0</p><br /><p>&#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160;ORDER BY p_entity.ENTITY_INCDE DESC</p><p>Au passage, je me suis permis de mettre les LEFT JOIN à la fin. Je trouve cela plus lisible (on est comme ça sûr dès la première lecture de la requête que les JOIN ne dépendent pas du LEFT JOIN).</p>]]></content>
